torchtitan on torch_tpu, applied by docker/Dockerfile.tpu at TORCHTITAN_COMMIT; rebase it whenever that commit moves.
`patch` skips this text. Each hunk, and where it should end up:

- fsdp.py `_cpu_offload_policy`: generic torch_tpu support (pinned copies deadlock against compiled
  activation-checkpointed blocks on TPU). Upstream to torchtitan.
- fsdp.py final norm in the root unit, not with the vocab-sized weight (tied unit, or lm_head when untied): TPU compile
  time (its dim / world elements misalign that unit's per-rank buffer; a Qwen3-4B trainer cold-compiled ~33 min before,
  ~6 min after). Upstream to torchtitan.
- tools/utils.py `_TpuDeviceModule`: generic torch_tpu support (torch.tpu refuses device calls from outside torch and
  lacks the memory-stats APIs torchtitan calls). Upstream to torchtitan as a torch.accelerator device module.
- distributed/utils.py `dtensor_rng_off_for_cpu_shards` around training_engine.py's init_weights: CPU-offloaded init
  on an accelerator mesh (torch 2.14's trunc_normal_ never returns: DTensor's RNG tracker restores the CPU RNG after
  every op; Qwen3.8-27B with the host optimizer hung in init_weights, 93 s after). Not TPU-specific. Backport of
  pytorch/torchtitan#6161: drop these two hunks once TORCHTITAN_COMMIT includes it.

FSDP's force-SUM reduction (tpu_dist has no PREMUL_SUM) lives in miles (TitanTrainer, Platform.premul_sum_reduce).

